    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grōmātĭcus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grūm-</span></b> ),
			a, um, adj.
		groma, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to field-surveying</i> or
				<i>castrametation.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">disciplina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Varr. 3, 52</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grōmā-tĭca</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grūm-</span></b> ),
				ae, f., <i>the art of
				field-surveying</i> or <i>castrametation</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Varr. 3,
			52</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grōmātĭci</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>writers on field-surveying</i>, Hyg. de Mun. Castr. §
			12.</div>
